{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-dq-squared","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-dq-squared","kind":"proposition","title":"Non-vanishing of $d_q^2$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-ext-deriv"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-dq-squared"],"tags":["exterior-derivative","deformation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.categorical_dq_squared","text":"categorical-dq-squared.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-dq-squared\"></a><p>The composition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2 = d_q \\circ d_q \\colon \\Omega^k(A) \\to \\Omega^{k+2}(A)</code> is given by</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  d_q^2\\alpha =  q^{-1}(1 - q^{-1})\\omega_V \\wedge_q [\\xi, \\alpha],</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\omega_V \\in \\Omega^2(A)</code> is the curvature of the weight decomposition and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[\\xi, \\alpha]</code> is the Lie derivative along the generator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>.</p>\n<p>The composition vanishes if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code> or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[\\xi, \\alpha] = 0</code>. For generic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\neq 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2 \\neq 0</code>, so the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed de Rham complex fails to be a cochain complex. On <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>-invariant horizontal forms, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q</code> reduces to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^{-1} d</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2 = 0</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.18.1"}
